@startuml
title Decorator / Wrapper (behavioral extension)

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Attach responsibilities to objects dynamically; flexible alternative to subclassing.

**Motivation**:
Need to add features to instances at runtime
(e.g. caching/logging/compression/encryption).

**Applicability**:
Need flexible, composable behavior enhancements per instance.

**Participants**:
Decorator wraps a Component and forwards/augments calls.

**Consequences**:
Pros: Composable features; per-instance variability; open/closed principle.
Cons: Many small objects; debugging stacked decorators can be tricky.

**Implementation Notes**:
Keep decorator interface consistent with component.
Consider ordering and idempotency of decorators.

**Known Uses**:
Java IO streams (BufferedInputStream, GZIPInputStream).
Servlet filters (decorator-like pipelines).

**Related Patterns**:
Composite, Adapter, Strategy, Chain of Responsibility.

endlegend

interface Component {
  +operation()
}

abstract class Decorator implements Component {
  -component : Component
  +operation()
}

class ConcreteComponent
class ConcreteDecoratorA
class ConcreteDecoratorB

Component <|.. ConcreteComponent
Decorator <|-- ConcreteDecoratorA
Decorator <|-- ConcreteDecoratorB
Decorator o-- Component
@enduml